          "Consolidate the white working-class homeowner base on economic security: property tax management, job quality, healthcare access, and whether state government is delivering on infrastructure and education investment. This constituency is materially stressed at $50,236 income and 16.1% college attainment, and they will reward a representative who delivers on concrete economic results.",
          "Engage the 24.3% renter constituency on cost-of-living issues — wages, housing affordability, childcare access, and whether the state is investing in economic opportunity for non-homeowners. Renters and younger adults are the most likely constituency to evaluate on material government performance rather than inherited partisanship, and their mobilization is the single greatest risk to the current margin.",
          "Recognize that an 88% result is not a durable supermajority but a reflection of current homeowner consolidation and minority disengagement; any credible challenger who mobilizes the 19% non-white constituency or activates renter economic concerns can move this margin significantly. The strategic task is not to celebrate the margin but to understand what holds it and to reinforce those foundations continuously."
