          "Engage the 25.58% Black constituency as full economic participants in the district's upper-middle-income community: messaging on homeownership protection, school quality, and professional opportunity resonates across racial lines here in a way that poverty-framed outreach does not and will not.",
          "Diagnose the 40% opposition before the next cycle: whether it is concentrated in predominantly Black precincts reflecting low engagement or suppressed turnout, or distributed among college-educated white homeowners with governance concerns, determines whether the 60% hold is durable or fragile — and the answer requires precinct-level analysis, not assumption.",
          "Treat the 30.1% college attainment rate as a governance-expectations signal: educated homeowners at nearly $90,000 median income scrutinize legislative competence and policy specifics, and a candidate who leads with cultural positioning over substantive local governance risks alienating the most persuadable high-propensity voters in the district."
