          "Anchor constituent service and legislative messaging in the specific material concerns of a $57,820-income, 17.9%-college-attainment district: workforce wages, rural healthcare access, public school funding, and the cost of basic services are the issues that generate genuine loyalty in this demographic profile.",
          "Build active, ongoing relationships with Black community institutions — churches, civic organizations, and local leaders — not as electoral insurance but as a governing obligation; the 18.4% Black population is too large to represent authentically through passive incumbency, and any future challenger will begin their campaign there.",
          "Engage the district's renters — 25.7% of households — with specific attention to housing affordability and workforce development; in a low-college-attainment, moderate-income district, renters are the constituency most exposed to economic volatility and most likely to respond to a challenger who speaks directly to their instability."
