          { name: "Abstract Ideological Positioning Disconnected from Material Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "With only 20.2% of adults holding college degrees, HD-19's constituency is not primarily engaged with abstract legislative or ideological debates — it is engaged with whether government is delivering on wages, healthcare, roads, and economic opportunity at the $68,850 income level where most households operate. A representative whose public communication and legislative emphasis is dominated by culture-war positioning or national partisan signaling at the expense of specific, deliverable local results risks appearing unresponsive to the kitchen-table concerns that define this district's political expectations. The 21.6% renter rate and 38.4 median age further suggest a cohort of younger, economically pressured adults who are the least forgiving of a representative whose priorities appear misaligned with their immediate material circumstances." }
