          "Engage the 26.36% white population and 1.92% Hispanic population with specific constituent attention rather than assuming they are politically invisible; in a 69.7% Black majority district, other communities' economic and social concerns can become neglected, but their material needs around housing, education, and employment are real.",
          "Use the absence of partisan pressure to invest in local problem-solving capacity — hiring constituent services staff, building relationships with Jackson's employers and educational institutions, and establishing office accessibility — that generates authentic loyalty based on results rather than inherited party affiliation."
