          { name: "Abstract Conservative Framing on Economic Issues", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district at $30,973 median income with 64.9% renters and 79.55% Black residents, abstract conservative positioning on housing, healthcare, education, or employment offers no solutions to the material conditions voters face. Framing that emphasizes market solutions, limited government, or 'opportunity' without concrete policy remedies for renter instability, healthcare access, or wage stagnation will fail to resonate with and may actively alienate a constituency evaluating on whether government is delivering real improvements in their daily economic security." }
