          "Engage the professional-class healthcare and retirement security agenda specifically — at 42.8 median age with high income and education, this constituency faces rising healthcare costs and retirement adequacy concerns that state policy directly affects; generic conservative positioning without specific remedies will lose credibility.",
          "Recognize that an unopposed 2023 win does not indicate absence of voter concern — 19.6% renters and potential economic anxiety even at higher income levels mean any successor should actively build relationships rather than assuming the unopposed result signals durable consolidation.",
          "Monitor and engage the ~3.6% demographic gap and any professional-class diversification in the district — affluent suburban constituencies can experience demographic evolution that shifts needs around language access, immigrant professional integration, or education quality for diverse populations without any change to overall partisan alignment."
