          "Engage the 21% Black constituency with authentic constituent attention and specific policy responses to economic mobility, healthcare access, and workforce development concerns — this is the single largest swing population in the district and the most likely source of a credible challenger if Democratic infrastructure rebuilds.",
          "Lead with working-class economic security messaging: at $55,563 median income with only 15.1% college education, this constituency evaluates on whether government delivers concrete benefits to their household economics, not on partisan identity or culture-war positioning.",
          "Build local governance presence and constituent service capacity that is visible and responsive; in a low-education rural district where media consumption is limited, direct constituent service and word-of-mouth reputation are the primary political currencies and the best defense against future challenges."
