          { name: "Abstract Partisan Messaging Without Material Progress", tag: "avoid", why: "Constituents earning $33K, renting at high rates, and lacking credential pathways evaluate their representative on concrete delivery — whether neighborhood conditions are improving, whether they or their neighbors have found better jobs, whether housing problems get solved. State-level partisan messaging disconnected from visible local improvement is electorally hollow in a district where material need is constant and pressing. Service delivery performance, not party identity messaging, determines electoral durability." }
