          "Build a concrete workforce development agenda: with only 9.8% college attainment, the district needs accessible post-secondary pathways through community colleges, apprenticeships, and employer partnerships that connect high school graduates to sustained employment at wages that support a family — and your representative should be able to name the specific programs and employers they are partnering with.",
          "Engage healthcare access with specificity: in a 77.66% Black district at $25K median income, Medicaid eligibility, clinic location and hours, and preventive care access are not abstract health policy — they determine whether families can afford to see a doctor; speak to the actual healthcare decisions facing your constituents, not partisan rhetoric about healthcare.",
          "Do not assume unopposed 2023 means strong constituent attachment: an unopposed result indicates no organized challenger emerged, not that constituents enthusiastically support the incumbent; any representative who campaigns as though 2023's lack of opposition signals durable electoral safety will be vulnerable to a credible challenger who focuses on concrete answers to housing, jobs, and healthcare."
