          "Build authentic engagement with the Black community (20.68%) through specific issue commitment: Medicaid expansion, education funding adequacy, criminal justice reform, and economic opportunity in majority-Black neighborhoods are the concrete governance concerns that activate Black voter participation — not generic outreach or token acknowledgment. In a district this young and economically constrained, a challenger who offers concrete answers on these issues can rapidly shift mobilization.",
          "Address working-class economic security directly: at $56,291 median income with 29.3% renting, the primary voter concern is whether state government is delivering on job creation, housing affordability, healthcare access, and public education quality. An incumbent who cannot articulate specific legislative accomplishments on these issues is vulnerable to a challenger who can.",
          "Understand that the incumbent's apparent dominance masks a district composition (young, working-class, 20% Black) that is not naturally aligned with Republican partisan identity — it is held by performance expectations and constituent relationships, not by inherited loyalty. Any challenger who invests in genuine community organizing in Black neighborhoods and among young renters can build the opposition coalition the 2023 election did not produce."
