          { name: "Taking the District's Racial Composition for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "With 23.93% Black and 71.72% white, the partisan stability of this district depends on how well the incumbent cultivates both communities and whether each perceives their concerns are being addressed. Generic appeals to 'all constituents' or absorbed minority outreach can leave both the Black community and working-class white community feeling their specific needs are not being heard. In a district at this income level where both communities face real economic pressures, targeted constituent service and visible policy attention to their concerns is not optional—it is the foundation of actual political durability." }
