          { name: "Ignoring Minority Population Representation", tag: "avoid", why: "The 6.46% demographic gap combined with 6.32% Hispanic and 6.08% Black populations means MS-HD-95 has roughly 18-20% non-majority constituents who are not meaningfully visible in the current political dialogue. Treating these populations as negligible — or failing to build specific constituent relationships with Hispanic, Black, and other minority communities in suburban settings — creates an opening for an alternative candidate to mobilize these voters as a constituency bloc. A legislator who serves only the 80% majority risks losing election when those 18-20% show up to vote as an organized group." }
