          { name: "Assuming Black Voter Demobilization or Monolithic Party Loyalty", tag: "avoid", why: "Campaigns that treat the Black community as a fixed Democratic base requiring no active engagement or assume Black voter turnout will remain suppressed are strategically vulnerable. At 26.21% of the district, the Black community is large enough that increased turnout (particularly around economic issues) or a candidate who offers specific answers on material concerns can substantially narrow the current margin. A representative who does not actively engage this constituency risks finding it mobilized against them in a future cycle." }
