          { name: "Treating Unopposed Victory as Durable Support", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed race produces 100% margins that have no relationship to genuine political durability; they conceal rather than reveal actual constituent satisfaction. An incumbent who campaigns as if 100% represents a safe majority is strategically blind to the specific economic concerns—property tax burden, healthcare cost, educational access—that are most likely to activate opposition in the next competitive cycle. In a district with 82.5% homeownership at $54,579 income, economic anxiety is not a theoretical concern; it is the daily material reality for the majority of voters." },
          { name: "Neglecting Black and Hispanic Constituencies Under the Assumption of Unopposed Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "The 14.25% Black and 2% Hispanic populations in MS-HD-106 have never voted under competitive conditions in this district, making them an unknown quantity in terms of voting behavior and constituent satisfaction. An incumbent who takes these communities for granted because there was no opponent in 2023 risks creating the opening for a challenger to organize them around specific unmet concerns—economic development, criminal justice responsiveness, healthcare access—that have gone unaddressed. Proactive constituent engagement with these communities is both an ethical governance obligation and essential electoral strategy." }
