          "Build specific Black community engagement: the 11.3% Black population has been invisible in unopposed governance, and real economic disparities in employment, homeownership, and healthcare access exist alongside the broader working-class economic story — address these with the same specificity offered to white constituents.",
          "Avoid framing this as a safe seat: unopposed victory is not a majority mandate — it is the outcome of the absence of opposition — and any candidate who campaigns assuming inherited voter loyalty rather than active constituent service will be vulnerable to an opponent who takes working-class economic concerns seriously."
