          { name: "Generic Progressive Messaging Detached from Material Economic Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "A district of older, property-holding homeowners at $69,674 income does not respond to abstract progressive ideology; it responds to whether government is protecting their economic interests and delivering concrete results on healthcare costs and property tax management. Democratic messaging in MS-HD-111 that emphasizes partisan positioning over concrete legislative results on aging homeowner economic security will struggle against a Republican challenger who makes these material concerns central to the campaign, potentially losing persuadable homeowners who vote on competence rather than party loyalty." }
