          { name: "Assuming Inherited Partisan Loyalty Rather Than Active Constituent Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "A 31.7-year median age, 58.4% renter rate, and below-average college attainment rate indicate a constituency that evaluates representatives on material delivery — whether government is actually improving their economic security and responding to their concrete needs — rather than on abstract partisan affiliation. Younger renters facing housing cost pressure, Black and Hispanic households seeking economic opportunity, and working-class families at $51,359 income will not grant automatic loyalty to any candidate; they will vote for whoever demonstrates they understand and are solving the problems that directly affect their lives. A representative who relies on partisan default rather than active engagement with these material concerns will find the seat vulnerable the moment a challenger appears with specific policy answers." }
