          "Build active relationships with Black and Hispanic communities rather than assuming they will default to any candidate: together they represent 33.5% of the district, and without specific engagement on economic opportunity, healthcare access, and community safety, they represent the swing vote in a district where the white majority is declining and younger voters evaluate on material delivery rather than inherited partisan loyalty.",
          "Develop a targeted economic agenda for younger adults (median age 31.7): wage growth, student debt management, healthcare access, and pathways to homeownership or stable rental futures are the material concerns that will drive turnout and candidate preference — not culture-war abstractions that are disconnected from younger voters' lived experience.",
          "Recognize that unopposed status in 2023 is electoral fragility, not strength: once a credible challenger emerges with specific messaging on housing, economic opportunity, and community investment, the current margin offers no buffer — only active constituent engagement and demonstrated delivery on material concerns will hold this seat."
