          "Engage the approximately 4.6% demographic gap (likely American Indian and multiracial residents) with specific constituent attention; in a district this heavily Republican, small shifts in turnout or preference among populations not prominently visible in the headline numbers can affect competitive dynamics in future cycles.",
          "Do not campaign this seat as though 77% reflects settled partisan loyalty—it reflects the current alignment of a working-class homeowner majority with Republican governance, which is durable only if that governance continues delivering on economic security concerns; any incumbent who assumes the margin and neglects constituent economic pressures risks unexpected competitive vulnerability."
