          { name: "Assuming Demographic Diversity Generates Partisan Loyalty", tag: "avoid", why: "MS-SD-9's demographic profile — 23.08% Black, 36.8% renters, median age 30.4, 43.5% college-educated — might appear to generate a naturally Democratic constituency. However, unopposed incumbency obscures whether these demographics are actually mobilized, whether their specific economic concerns are being addressed, or whether dissatisfaction exists. A candidate who campaigns on the assumption that Black voters, young renters, and college-educated professionals will automatically consolidate without offering concrete answers to their material concerns (housing affordability, job quality, healthcare) will find that demographic diversity alone is insufficient to hold or win the seat against a credible challenger who engages these communities' actual priorities." }
