          "Consolidate the Black vote through healthcare access and community investment: the 34.79% Black population is the incumbent's base, but consolidation requires demonstrating specific results on Medicaid access, maternal and infant health, and investment in historically underserved communities—not generic Democratic positioning.",
          "Retain and expand white working-class support by addressing economic anxiety with specificity: the 57.38% white plurality at $57,746 income and 40.3 median age is economically stressed; Republican messaging will exploit that stress unless the Democrat offers concrete results on job quality, healthcare costs, and whether government is delivering for working families.",
