          "Lead with working-class economic security across racial lines: the $65,100 income, 28.9% college attainment, and 29% renter rate define a constituency for whom housing affordability, healthcare access, wage growth, and job training are the material governance concerns — a message that resonates with both white and Black working-class voters is the foundation of any durable majority.",
          "Build genuine relationships with Black community institutions and leadership: at 28.75% of the district, the Black population is a substantial constituency whose civic infrastructure, churches, and organizations are the connective tissue of community life — engagement here cannot be episodic or campaign-timed; it requires ongoing partnership and visible reinvestment in community priorities.",
          "Engage renters and younger adults on housing: the 29% renter rate in a district with median age 37.1 signals a population facing housing cost pressure in an economic context where income growth has not kept pace with rent — addressing renter protections, affordable housing development, and housing cost containment directly differentiates a candidate and mobilizes a constituency often invisible in homeowner-focused campaigns."
