          "Build a concrete economic security agenda: at $51,991 median income, 17.1% college attainment, and 24.8% renter rate, MS-SD-18 is a working-class constituency for whom healthcare costs, housing stability, and wage dynamics are material governance concerns — abstract partisan messaging will not hold this seat if a challenger offers specific economic remedies.",
          "Engage the 27% Black population as a constituent base, not a presumed voting bloc: whether the Black community participates and how it votes depends on whether the incumbent or challenger has earned their trust through specific constituent attention on the issues that matter to Black households — economic mobility, healthcare access, and equitable public investment — rather than assumed loyalty.",
          "Recognize that 24.8% renters represent a constituency with different economic stakes than the homeowner majority: housing costs, tenant protections, and the cost-of-living burden on lower-income renters are governance issues that do not disappear because they are not always visible in partisan analysis — a durable legislative agenda must address them."
