          { name: "Working-Family Economic Security and Concrete Delivery", tag: "lean-into", why: "At $43,148 median household income and 40.8% renter rate, MS-SD-27 constituents face daily financial stress around housing costs, school quality, and employment opportunity — not abstract partisan concerns. The unopposed 2023 result reflects Democratic alignment, but constituent loyalty is conditional on perceiving that their representative is actively solving the material problems that shape their lives: school funding, job access, affordable housing, and public safety. An incumbent who makes tangible delivery on these concerns central to their legislative identity and constituent communication is substantially less vulnerable to primary challenge or general-election mobilization than one who treats the Democratic lean as a permanent buffer." },
          { name: "Educational Access and Economic Mobility for Young Adults", tag: "lean-into", why: "The 27.2% college-attainment rate in a district with 37.2 median age describes a constituency where educational barriers to economic mobility are a real and present constraint on household earnings potential. Public school funding, workforce training access, higher education affordability, and the pipeline from education to employment are the concrete policy areas where a state legislator can materially affect a young adult's ability to earn above the district's current median income. A legislative record focused on expanding educational access and opportunity is both good governance for the district and strong electoral positioning because it addresses the material concerns that shape constituent decision-making." },
          { name: "Preventing Incumbent Complacency and Constituent Disengagement", tag: "careful", why: "An unopposed incumbent faces a specific governance risk: the temptation to treat election security as equivalent to constituent satisfaction, and to allow constituent engagement and responsive service to atrophy if perceived as unnecessary for re-election. In a district where 32% of voters did not vote in the 2023 unopposed election, there is a latent pool of potential voters who could be mobilized by a credible challenger with a message focused on service delivery and responsiveness. The incumbent's strategic requirement is to invest in sustained constituent engagement, visible problem-solving in neighborhoods, and responsive service delivery as baseline governance practice — not as a tactical re-election calculation, but as the work required to hold this seat if competition emerges." },
          { name: "Treating Democratic Lean as Permanent Electoral Insurance", tag: "avoid", why: "MS-SD-27's 100% Democratic result in 2023 reflects genuine party alignment, but alignment is not permanence — particularly when a district is simultaneously characterized by economic stress, underfunded schools, and housing insecurity. An incumbent who campaigns as though the Democratic margin is a permanent buffer, rather than a consequence of current constituent preference for Democratic governance, risks being surprised by a challenger who mobilizes dissatisfaction with service delivery and offers a credible message about problem-solving. The unopposed 2023 result is not evidence of safety; it is evidence of current electoral advantage that requires active constituent engagement to maintain." },
          { name: "Allowing Constituent Service Infrastructure to Atrophy", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where working families face $43,148 median income and housing cost burden, constituent service — responsive help with public benefits, housing applications, school placement, utility disputes, and other daily problems that press low-income households — is not a peripheral part of representation; it is core to whether constituents perceive their representative as actually working for them. An incumbent who allows constituent service operations to become understaffed or inefficient, or who reduces visible presence in neighborhoods and community spaces, is creating the conditions for a challenger to successfully argue that the incumbent is out of touch with constituent needs. Sustained, high-quality constituent service is both good governance and the operational foundation for holding this seat." }
