          "Engage the renter-majority constituency (53.8%) with specific housing policy: tenant protections, affordable housing development, predatory lending regulation, and whether state housing policy is protecting the district's economically vulnerable families from displacement. This is not an abstract issue — it is the survival question for most households in MS-SD-28.",
