          { name: "Neglecting Local Constituent Relationship-Building in Favor of Partisan Positioning", tag: "avoid", why: "A district this heavily Republican can tempt legislators to treat incumbency as sufficient and to neglect the active constituent engagement and relationship-building that converts electoral dominance into genuine safety. In a community of older homeowners with specific economic concerns and a small but present minority constituency, absence of personal constituent attention—town halls, service responsiveness, acknowledgment of community needs—creates the opening for an opposition candidate to build a 'representative who actually listens' narrative that resonates even in Republican territory." }
